lor:#dbdbdb;border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">321,974&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#dbdbdb;border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#dbdbdb;padding:0 1pt"/><td style="background-color:#dbdbdb;border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#dbdbdb;border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">325,680&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#dbdbdb;border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/></tr></table></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:7pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">(1) Fiscal year 2021 includes the impact of the 53-week year</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:14pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Restaurant-Level&#160;Margin </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Restaurant-Level&#160;Margin is defined as company restaurant sales less restaurant operating costs (food and packaging, labor, and occupancy costs) and is neither required by, nor presented in accordance with GAAP. Restaurant-Level&#160;Margin excludes revenues and expenses of our franchise operations and certain costs, such as selling, general, and administrative expenses, pre-opening costs, depreciation and amortization, other operating expense (income), net, gains or losses on the sale of company-operated restaurants, and other costs that are considered normal operating costs. As such, Restaurant-Level&#160;Margin is not indicative of the overall results of the Company and does not accrue directly to the benefit of shareholders because of the exclusion of corporate-level expenses. Restaurant-Level&#160;Margin should be considered as a supplement to, not as a substitute for, analysis of results as reported under GAAP or other similarly titled measures of other companies. The Company is presenting Restaurant-Level&#160;Margin because it believes that it provides a meaningful supplement to net earnings of the Company&#8217;s core business operating results, as well as a comparison to those of other similar companies. Management utilizes Restaurant-Level&#160;Margin as a key performance indicator to evaluate the profitability of company-owned restaurants. </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:5pt"><span><br/></span></div><div style="height:36pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div><span style="color:#474747;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:100%">A-1</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">  </span><span style="color:#f01639;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:100%">JACK IN THE BOX INC.</span><span style="color:#f01639;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">&#8201;|&#8201;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:100%">2025</span><span style="